Full suite green: **259 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.

## What I changed

The `POST /api/owners` pipeline already had a `RejectDuplicateOwner` step (from the earlier cp02 rule). It only rejected when both **last name and telephone** matched an existing owner, scanning via `findByLastName`. The new rule is broader: reject when the **telephone alone** collides with **any** other owner.

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RejectDuplicateOwner.java` now scans all owners via `findAll()` and throws `ConflictException` on any telephone match (excluding the owner itself by id):

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws ConflictException {
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (!Objects.equals(existing.getId(), owner.getId())
            && Objects.equals(owner.getTelephone(), existing.getTelephone())) {
            throw new ConflictException("An owner with the same telephone already exists");
        }
    }
}
```

`ConflictException` is already mapped to a **409** by the existing escalation handler (`escalation/…ConflictException.yml`), and the YAML pipeline was unchanged.

This telephone-only rule is a superset of the old last-name-AND-telephone rule, so the existing cp02 tests still pass, and the new cp03 tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephones`) now pass too.
